render.ts build() writes whatever a .njk renders, so a rule gated entirely by {% if vars.x %} lands as an empty .claude/rules/<name>.md. Wanted: when an item's main file (rule/agent .md, skill SKILL.md) renders to whitespace only, the item counts as 'not applicable' for this scope: nothing is written, an already-installed copy is removed via the lock, and status/report shows it as skipped (not as error). Enables a rule set where vars switch individual rules on/off per user/project/local.

Settle in the spec (§5/§6.1): exact emptiness test (whitespace only; frontmatter-only counts as empty?), behaviour for skills with extra files when SKILL.md is empty (skip whole item), interaction with --force/conflict handling. Regression tests: gated-off rule not written; toggling var off removes the installed file; toggling back on reinstalls.
Target: skilletor-worker + skilletor-skill-author for docs. Pairs well with the wildcard ticket.

